// # sec/landlock — Kernel-Mediated FS Containment
//
// Logline: The Landlock FS sandbox, the platform-detecting probe, and the live-RAM proc_mem reader gated by Landlock (Pillar 9).
//
// Beats:
//   1. landlock/landlock.h — the OoLandlockStatus enum and rule flags (kept at top level for the public C API).
//   2. landlock/landlock.c — orchestrator: the Landlock rule construction and apply.
//   3. landlock/landlock_restrict.c — oo_landlock_restrict_fd (the per-fd restrict primitive).
//   4. sandbox/sandbox.c — orchestrator: the platform-detecting probe (Landlock on Linux, fail-closed elsewhere).
//   5. sandbox/sandbox.h — the OoLandlockSandbox type (kept at top level for the public C API).
//   6. sandbox/sandbox_c.c — the v2.2.0 sys_cap-gated oo_sandbox_c_* C-ABI backdoor (preserved).
//   7. sandbox/sandbox_config.c — the OoLandlockConfig builder.
//   8. sandbox/sandbox_matrix.c — the per-domain (FsRead, FsWrite, Net, ...) rule matrix.
//   9. proc_mem.c — the live-RAM reader; gated by Landlock + cap.
//
// v2.3.0 file split: the original 296-line landlock.c was split into
// landlock/ subdir (2 files), and the original 638-line sandbox.c was
// split into sandbox/ subdir (4 files). The split is functional
// (one Landlock concern per file). The platform-detect probe stays
// in sandbox.c (the orchestrator).
//
// ──▓▓ sec/landlock ANCHOR ──▓▓──
// :: Pillar 9 — kernel-mediated, not userland shim ::
